The scenario `env/env_0069_managed_it_services_provider` is finished. All three delivery conditions hold: every difficulty passed its policy audit, every published product passed its KB audit, and the whole-scenario `validate_scenario` check returns **VALID** with no warnings or errors.

**What was built:** the company is Stratton Bay Technology Partners. There are 7 products and 5 difficulties with 2 tasks each, so 10 tasks.

| Difficulty | Product | Policy audit | KB audit |
|---|---|---|---|
| managed_services_agreements | ClearPath Managed IT Services (`managed`) | PASS, round 9 | PASS, round 3 |
| microsoft_365_subscriptions | Microsoft 365 subscriptions (`licensing`) | PASS, round 11 | PASS, round 2 |
| prepaid_service_hours | TimeBank prepaid hours (`timebank`) | PASS, round 14 | PASS, round 2 |
| project_engagements | Professional services projects (`project`) | PASS, round 9 | PASS, round 3 |
| hardware_procurement_orders | Hardware procurement (`hardware`) | PASS, round 7 | PASS, round 4 |

- **Unaudited products:** `security` (Sentinel) and `backup` (Continuum) are base products that no difficulty claims. Per the skill they were rendered and passed their render gate but were never audited.
- **Gates at the end:** all 5 difficulties pass their 7 instantiation gates and the traceability check, and all 7 products print DOCS OK.
- **Identifier clash check:** I scanned phone, email, EIN digits, PIN, organisation name and contact name across all customer records. There were no duplicates.

**Known issues accepted without a fix:**
- **Base-text wording:** a few wording issues in the frozen base product text are left as they are and logged in the worklog. One example is a lifecycle sentence on reinstatement that disagrees with the rule's fee timing. None changes a scored value.
- **Placement-only notes:** a few document notes about where a sentence sits were deliberately not sent back for rework, and the decisions are logged. One example is the coverage sentence in the licensing cancellation computation document.
- **Bulky files:** the `.audit_views/` directory stays in place because the audit reports cite it by hash. The worklog also keeps the scratch `plan.md` files.

**Costs of the run:** about 8 account-limit cuts. Every interrupted call was checked on disk and then resumed or re-sent. I made one bad routing call myself: I told the M365 reworker to post 0.00 billing lines. That contradicted the frozen schema, where amounts must be positive, and cost one extra round to replace.

I saved this run's lessons to memory: check the schema before proposing a route, re-price other products' seed rows in one bounded pass, and seed each holding's history from signing.

The full timeline is in `env/env_0069_managed_it_services_provider/worklog.md`, which ends with `DELIVERED`.
